Z||000006||rogergarrison||12-27-2001||02:09 PM||||Thats an AMC Hornet. The original Hudson Hornets were cool cars. They won tons of races in Nascar too in the early years against the ford and olds V8s. On a slightly different note, I had a  63 Plymouth Valiant with a 225 ci slant 6. It had split dual exhaust and an Offenhauser intake with 2 4bbls.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 12-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||CoolBlue87GT||12-27-2001||02:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>Thats an AMC Hornet...<P> I had a  63 Plymouth Valiant with a 225 ci slant 6. It had split dual exhaust and an Offenhauser intake with 2 4bbls.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Wow, 2 4bbls ?  That sounds neat. Man, mine only had one 2bbl.<P>Yes your right AMC, w/258 6cyl<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/junk9.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000008||rogergarrison||12-27-2001||05:47 PM||||Man, thats got to be a rare model.<P>those headers look pretty complex, custom or did someone really sell them like that?<P>Ya cool, all were 2 bbl from factory except the 273 powerpack with 1 carter AFB. Mine was aftermarket all the way. My first fast ride, swapped it out for a 426 Hemi from a wrecked Super Bee.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 12-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Nashco||12-28-2001||04:13 AM||||A friend of mine has a 75 Jeep CJ-5 with the 258 in it.  He's got just about everything modded except for the transmission right now.  He's got a header with full dual exhaust (gurgly flowmasters, of course <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">)...that header setup is readily available for the jeeps.  They do look pretty cool/fancy, but they are a b!tch to install and keep from getting leaks compared to some other setups.  With the low RPM cam he has it hates to rev high, but has an amazing amount of torque!!!!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000010||CoolBlue87GT||12-28-2001||11:20 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Nashco:<BR><B>A friend of mine has a 75 Jeep CJ-5 with the 258 in it.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Yes, you are right, this set was made by Hooker Headers. <P>It was a two piece set. 1st half took the 1st 4 cyl, the 2nd took the last two cly.<P>Now the two half connected with the 'tube' for the 4th cyl sliding into a 'tube' going to the 2nd collecter.<P>So each collecter handled 3 cyl. To describe it, sounds weird, but believe me, it sounded good.<P>I always loved starting it, and hearing the 3" dual exhaust burbling as it warmed up. Sounded like it had a V8. Many friends were impressed.<P>-Always needed to warm to up a bit on cold starts, as the choke assembly was lost the to header setup. <P>This set never had problems w/leaks. The hardest part was keeping the high temp white paint on them. Finaly found some good stuff seen here.<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/junk7.jpg">   <p>[This message has been edited by CoolBlue87GT (edited 12-28-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000011||rockcrawl||12-28-2001||09:06 PM||||I'm helping a friend build up a '79 CJ5 with the AMC 258. We chose a single outlet Borla header because it's the only stainless steel one we could find. It also has a Crane cam and a Clifford four barrel intake (6=8), we're fitting a GM TBI system to it.||||reg||1
